ATTACK #3 -- NAME_MAX arithmetic. Read storage.go: StagingSuffix = ".tmp-"
(5 bytes, unconditional literal). Read GOROOT src/os/tempfile.go: CreateTemp's
random suffix is `itoa.Uitoa(uint(uint32(runtime_rand())))` -- unpadded
decimal, length >= 1 always (even value 0 renders as "0"), so worst case adds
only 1 byte. With base=255 bytes exactly, the staging name's fixed prefix
alone (255 + len(".tmp-") = 260) already exceeds NAME_MAX=255 before any
random digits are appended -- the mechanism does not depend on the random
suffix's length at all, so it cannot flake regardless of runtime_rand()'s
output. PATH_MAX: t.TempDir() nesting depth doesn't threaten this (ENAMETOOLONG
here is a per-component check, and total path length from /tmp is nowhere
near 4096). This host is ext4 (confirmed above); tmpfs shares the same
255-byte NAME_MAX on Linux. Portability to non-Linux (windows) is explicitly
skipped by the test itself. No fragility found.

